    apply: "Pray about whom to approach as an accountability partner and ask them this week. Agree on a regular time and questions. Confess something you have been hiding to God and to a trusted person if appropriate. Memorise James 5:16.",
    activity: "Read 1 John 1:5-9 and James 5:13-16. Discuss the connection between light and fellowship. Write a list of good accountability questions. Practise how to respond to a confession in a role-play. Pray for honesty and safe community.",
    takeHome: "Read 1 John 1, James 5:13-20, Proverbs 28 and Galatians 6:1-10. Write accountability questions. Memorise James 5:16.",
    prayer: "Thank God for light and forgiveness. Ask for courage to be honest and for safe friends. Pray for those who feel alone in their struggle.",
    teacher: "Do not require public confession. Encourage private conversations with trusted leaders. Set boundaries and follow safeguarding procedures: accountability partners should be of the same sex, and minors should be accountable to appropriate adults with oversight. Report abuse or crime as required.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners how confession and community help in the fight against sin.",
    mcq1: ["What does James 5:16 say?", ["Confess your sins to one another and pray for one another, that you may be healed", "Hide your sins", "Never pray", "Tell everyone"], 0, "Confess and pray."],
